{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1354583-are-left-handed-paths-acceptable-for-ascension","id":1354583,"title":"Are Left handed Paths acceptable for Ascension?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-12T09:04:12-08:00","id":1354583,"title":"Are Left handed Paths acceptable for Ascension?","content":"Or are they just slippery slopes into Nephandidom? After reading Book of the Fallen I am not sure there's room for them as anything but a Nephandic fifth Column but I may be misreading both types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T15:31:42-08:00","id":1354681,"title":"","content":"They are quite fine for Ascension in theory. *Nobody* knows what the correct path to ascension is - and there are some really nasty Mages, as well as rough, amoral magickal practices and magical traditions out there that have absolutely nothing to do with Nephandi. A savage magickal practice has nothing to do with being drawn closer to being a Nephandus - becoming a Nephandus requires a quite nihilistic worldview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T15:43:23-08:00","id":1354685,"title":"","content":"A LOT of Cultists of Ecstasy can be seen as following a lefthand path. Also Tibeten Akashics who practice Tantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T16:22:23-08:00","id":1354692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1354583-are-left-handed-paths-acceptable-for-ascension?p=1354681#post1354681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are quite fine for Ascension in theory. *Nobody* knows what the correct path to ascension is - and there are some really nasty Mages, as well as rough, amoral magickal practices and magical traditions out there that have absolutely nothing to do with Nephandi. A savage magickal practice has nothing to do with being drawn closer to being a Nephandus - becoming a Nephandus requires a quite nihilistic worldview.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personal Descension is a valid path for the Nephandus. Someone who just doesn't care about what they do to others as long as they can become one with the outerdark. That starts to look ALOT like Lefthand personal Ascension from the outside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T22:54:24-08:00","id":1354725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1354583-are-left-handed-paths-acceptable-for-ascension?p=1354692#post1354692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personal Descension is a valid path for the Nephandus.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is! Even the paths that the Marauders take might lead some of them to Ascension.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T16:01:03-08:00","id":1354935,"title":"","content":"The Left-hand/Right-hand dichotomy is an artificial distinction imposed on Eastern philosophies by Western esoterists, to make such practices fit into Western norms. Characters from the Cult of Ecstasy, Euthanatos, and Akashayana would probably answer the question &quot;what is the Left Hand Path?&quot; with &quot;there is no such thing&quot;. There are practices, each with their own particulars, goals, and spiritual worth.<br /> <br /> Yes, there is a right and wrong way to do Magick, of course, but it's not as simple as Right and Left, respectively. If we're talking about Nephandi or even non-Fallen &quot;dark mages&quot;, the &quot;Right Hand Path&quot; can be just as easily bent towards evil as the &quot;Left Hand&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 12-14-2019, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T16:46:43-08:00","id":1354941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1354583-are-left-handed-paths-acceptable-for-ascension?p=1354935#post1354935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Left-hand/Right-hand dichotomy is an artificial distinction imposed on Eastern philosophies by Western esoterists, to make such practices fit into Western norms. Characters from the Cult of Ecstasy, Euthanatos, and Akashayana would probably answer the question &quot;what is the Left Hand Path?&quot; with &quot;there is no such thing&quot;. There are practices, each with their own particulars, goals, and spiritual worth.<br /> <br /> Yes, there is a right and wrong way to do Magick, of course, but it's not as simple as Right and Left, respectively. If we're talking about Nephandi or even non-Fallen &quot;dark mages&quot;, the &quot;Right Hand Path&quot; can be just as easily bent towards evil as the &quot;Left Hand&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The question is whether &quot;Right Hand Paths&quot; can lead to evil. The question is whether or not What is generally categorized as Left handed paths can lead anywhere but Nephandidom. The Book of the Fallen took alot of what I would have read as left hand types and said &quot;these are Nephandi&quot; Nephandi doen't even have to burn the world down they can now be hermits of wickedness..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T00:21:16-08:00","id":1355139,"title":"","content":"And the answer is: &quot;no one knows&quot;. Tradition mages don't know how to achieve Ascension, and what Ascension entails. There is no clear, repeatable process by which a traditions mage can Ascend. Some people threw shit at the wall and some of it stuck, and those people are not around to tell us what it was exactly. So any and all information that mages have is speculative. I'm sure if you asked a mage their answer would be &quot;no, left-hand paths don't lead to ascension&quot; because such is the paradigm and worldview in which tradition mages operate. But that's not necessarily true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T01:17:12-08:00","id":1355146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1354583-are-left-handed-paths-acceptable-for-ascension?p=1355139#post1355139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the answer is: &quot;no one knows&quot;. Tradition mages don't know how to achieve Ascension, and what Ascension entails. There is no clear, repeatable process by which a traditions mage can Ascend. Some people threw shit at the wall and some of it stuck, and those people are not around to tell us what it was exactly. So any and all information that mages have is speculative. I'm sure if you asked a mage their answer would be &quot;no, left-hand paths don't lead to ascension&quot; because such is the paradigm and worldview in which tradition mages operate. But that's not necessarily true.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am not asking a theoretical mage in their opinion. I am asking if Left handed paths are valid as presented as of m20 and the book of the Fallen or if they are functionally a 5th column in the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T03:00:42-08:00","id":1355154,"title":"","content":"No, &quot;left-handpaths&quot; are not immediate 5th columns. Yes, they are a valid path to ascension and not just &quot;nephandidom&quot;. If anything, their unorthodox nature requires more care to avoid that, but any path can lead to fall. It's not in normal practice, but in intent, where a mage Falls, and that in turn twists normal practice into a grotesque parody.<br /> I'm failing to see how previous comments didn't address this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","user":"El Barto","date":". 12-16-2019, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T06:28:46-08:00","id":1355170,"title":"","content":"Before we continue, it might be helpful to dispel confusion about what we're discussing. So to Lian, I request what every college professor says when grading a paper: <i>Define Your Terms</i>.<br /> <br /> What does the &quot;Left Hand Path&quot; <i>mean</i> to you? What does it entail? Setting aside whether its Nephandic, what even IS Left-Hand Path practice?<br /> <br /> Depending on what your definition is, we can then tell you what OUR definitions are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T06:54:08-08:00","id":1355174,"title":"","content":"After having considered the question for a hot minute, I went and checked the M20 core book. Just to refresh my memory about what the Mage books have to say about the question, which is the most pertinent &quot;official&quot; ruling on the matter.<br /> <br /> It reminded me that M20's Focus system makes a distinction between so-called &quot;Left Hand Path&quot; Practices - Chaos Magick, Crazy Wisdom, Witchcraft, and Yoga - and the Practice of <i>Maleficia</i>, the explicitly evil path of the Nephandus, Infernalist, and more general &quot;dark mage&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not every &quot;sex, drugs, and rock n' roll&quot; Practice is inherently evil. Nor does any Practice have a monopoly on magick being used for harmful ends, to ill intent.<br /> <br /> I would also be remiss if I failed to quote the sidebar directly addressing the matter of Left and Right Hand Paths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Left- And Right-Hand Paths (M20 p. 574)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Originally named by Europeans trying to differentiate between separate approaches to Tantric practices, the terms Left- Hand Path and Right-Hand Path have come to reflect an outlaw approach to mysticism and a reverent approach to it, respectively. Supposedly, Left-Hand mystics favor sensuality, hedonism, intoxication, and other forms of disreputable bliss, whereas Right-Hand adherents prefer asceticism, reverence, denial, and other forms of disciplined devotion.<br /> <br /> In truth, mystic practices (especially Tantra) are more complex than that simplified (and westernized) division between<br /> so-called bad and good behaviors. Even so, the distinction between Left- and Right-Hand approaches crops up a lot when people talk about crazy wisdom, witchcraft, chaos magick, and other practices that include socially questionable activities alongside socially approved ones.<br /> <br /> Certainly, some activities are more destructive than others, and magick does have consequences, like Resonance, that reach further than the moment of that act. Still, the division of Left- and Right-Hand magick tends to drop a Christianized gloss on practices that might be far older than Christianity and lack its simplistic bad/ good moral polarity. Some modern mages employ that term as shorthand for their approach, but others avoid its easy answers to complicated questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}